#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# difference_root

#% text
# `difference_root(f)` stands for the sequence defined by `f(y, n)`: a list of a linear recurrence for y(n) and enough initial values. `difference_root(f)(k)` gives its k-th term.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Terms at integers are computed by running the recurrence forward with `recurrence_table`; a list of integers gives a list of terms. Symbolic parameters stay in the terms, which are expanded.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
difference_root((y, k) => [y(k + 2) == y(k + 1) + y(k), y(0) == 0, y(1) == 1])(20)
#% output
#= 6765

#% cell
difference_root((y, k) => [y(k + 1) == (k + 1)*y(k), y(1) == 1])([3, 5, 10])
#% output
#= [6, 120, 3628800]

#% cell
difference_root((y, k) => [y(k + 2) == x*y(k + 1) - (k + 1)*y(k), y(0) == 1, y(1) == 1])(4)
#% output
#= 3 - 5*x - x^2 + x^3

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `differential_root`, `recurrence_table`, `r_solve`
